      "body": "[bp-review T6] Blueprint changes for SmoothPrimeRegularity + indeterminacy_codimGe2 are mathematically sound; two minor findings to tidy.\n\nCORE VERDICT: PASS. The 7 new nodes in subsec:smooth_prime_regularity all have correct 1-to-1 Lean pins (Polynomial.step_height_trdeg_of_isPrime, MvPolynomial.exists_le_trdeg_and_natCard_le_height_add, Algebra.IsStandardSmoothOfRelativeDimension.exists_le_trdeg_and_natCast_le_height_add, Algebra.rank_kaehlerDifferential_eq_trdeg, finrank_cotangentSpace_add_finrank_kaehler_residueField, isRegularLocalRing_of_isLocalization_atPrime_of_isStandardSmooth_of_perfectField). SmoothPrimeRegularity.lean and StandardSmoothDimension.lean are both sorry-free and compiled (oleans present); signatures match the LaTeX (hypotheses, trdeg/height directions, conormal identity, perfect-field/EssFiniteType assumptions all correct). All \\uses targets on changed nodes resolve; no dangling refs to the ~9 removed MvPolynomial/submersive substrate labels. The rewritten smooth_to_regular_local_ring proof is now pure and routes correctly through thm:standard_smooth_regular_at_prime.\n\nLEANOK HONESTY: correct. thm:indeterminacy_codimGe2 pins indeterminacy_codimGe2_of_smooth_of_complete (CodimOneExtension.lean:1374, body = sorry); node marks \\leanok on the STATEMENT line only, proof block has NO \\leanok. Same for thm:codim_one_extension (Lean sorry, not \\leanok). Honest per statement-level convention.\n\nFINDING 1 (math-purity, minor): The rewritten narrative subsections in Albanese_CodimOneExtension.tex (subsec:codim1_substrate_lemmas and the 'superseded decomposition' paragraph) still leak implementation/project history in ADDED lines: commit hash 'b80f227', 'proved axiom-clean', 'removed as dead code', Lean filename 'StandardSmoothDimension.lean'. The run greatly reduced this (-894 lines) but did not fully purge it. Non-node prose; pre-existing pattern.\n\nFINDING 2 (dead placeholder pins, minor): Now off the critical path (dropped from smooth_to_regular_local_ring \\uses), the two nodes lem:stage6_regular_stalk_assembly and lem:smooth_algebra_krull_dim_formula have \\lean{} pins (AlgebraicGeometry.TODO.stage6_regular_stalk_assembly and Algebra.IsStandardSmoothOfRelativeDimension.ringKrullDim_localization_eq_relativeDimension) that do NOT resolve to any Lean declaration (absent from source at HEAD and now; only listed in blueprint/lean_decls). They do not create dangling DAG edges and are correctly NOT \\leanok, but they break 1-to-1 correspondence (pin -> nonexistent decl) and are superseded by the arbitrary-prime route. Candidates for removal.\n\nNOTE (not a finding): thm:standard_smooth_regular_at_prime LaTeX says 'standard-smooth of relative dimension n' while the Lean uses [Algebra.IsStandardSmooth k S] with n derived internally; conclusion unaffected, acceptable.",
